# 📚 DermAI V2 Documentation Rules

## 🎯 Fundamental Principle
**`spec.md` is the central hub** that summarizes **ALL** application specifics and references **ALL** documentation.

## 📁 Mandatory Documentation Structure

### **Document Location**
- **ALL** specification documents must be in `/docs/`
- **NO** specification `.md` files at the project root (except the project `README.md`)
- **FORBIDDEN** to create temporary correction/changelog documents

### **Core Documents Allowed in `/docs/`**
1. **spec.md** — Central hub, complete app summary
2. **architecture-database.md** — Database architecture
3. **planning-dermai-v2.md** — Roadmap and planning
4. **monetization-strategy.md** — Business strategy and revenue
5. **dermatological-logic.md** — Dermatological business logic
6. **educational-interface.md** — User educational interface
7. **dermai-diagnostic-improvement-strategy.md** — AI improvement
8. **README.md** — Documentation navigation index

## 🚨 Strict Creation Rules

### **BEFORE creating a new document:**
1. **MANDATORY:** Check if the information can be integrated into an existing document
2. **IF a NEW DOCUMENT is necessary:**
   - **First**, create the section in `spec.md` that references this new document
   - Explain in `spec.md` why this separate document is needed
   - Add the link in `docs/README.md` under the appropriate section

### **Forbidden Document Types:**
❌ `CORRECTION_*.md` — Integrate directly into code or the main doc  
❌ `FIX_*.md` — Fix directly; no intermediate documentation  
❌ `CHANGELOG_*.md` — Use git commits and integrate into the main doc  
❌ `SUMMARY_*.md` — Summarize within the relevant main document  
❌ `IMPLEMENTATION_*.md` — Document in the technical section of `spec.md`  
❌ `UPDATE_*.md` — Update the main document directly  
❌ Any temporary correction or working file

### **Allowed Cases for a NEW Document:**
✅ **New major feature** (e.g., User dashboard)  
✅ **New technical subsystem** (e.g., Payment system)  
✅ **New external integration** (e.g., Shopify API)  
✅ **New business strategy** (e.g., SaaS model)

## 📝 Mandatory Procedure for a New Feature

### **Step 1: Update `spec.md`**
```markdown
## X. [NEW] Feature Name

### X.1. Overview
[Short description of the feature]

### X.2. Technical Architecture
[Technical summary]

### X.3. Detailed Documentation
See [feature-name.md](./feature-name.md) for full specifications.
```

### **Step 2: Create Detailed Document**
- Name: `docs/feature-name.md`
- Required structure:
```markdown
# Feature Name

## Overview
[Link to DermAI ecosystem]

## Technical Specifications
[Full details]

## Integration
[How it integrates with existing systems]
```

### **Step 3: Update `README.md`**
Add it in the appropriate section of `docs/README.md`

## 🛠️ Modification Rules

### **Modifying Existing Content:**
- Edit the relevant main document **directly**
- **No** intermediate correction document
- For major changes: note it in the relevant section of `spec.md`

### **Bug/Issue Fixes:**
- Fix the code directly
- If it impacts architecture: update `spec.md`
- **No** separate correction document

### **UX/UI Improvements:**
- If minor: no documentation
- If major: section in `spec.md` + update the relevant document

## 🎯 Responsibilities per Document

### **`spec.md` must include:**
- Complete application overview
- All features (summary)
- Global technical architecture
- Full technology stack
- Deployment configuration
- References to **ALL** other documents

### **Specialized documents include:**
- Deep, domain-specific details
- Precise technical specs
- Examples and use cases
- Specific procedures

## ⚠️ Automatic Sanctions

If these rules are not followed:
1. **Misplaced document** → Move immediately to `/docs/`
2. **Temporary document** → Merge its content and delete it
3. **`spec.md` not updated** → Add the required reference
4. **Duplicated information** → Consolidate into the main document

## 🔄 Documentation Maintenance

### **Mandatory monthly review:**
- Ensure `spec.md` references everything
- Delete obsolete documents
- Consolidate scattered information
- Update links and references

### **Before each major release:**
- Full validation of `spec.md`
- Check consistency across documents
- Update examples and procedures

## 📊 Concrete Example

**❌ BAD:**
```
/DASHBOARD_IMPLEMENTATION.md
/USER_PROFILE_FIXES.md
/PAYMENT_SYSTEM_DRAFT.md
```

**✅ GOOD:**
```
/docs/spec.md (with a Dashboard section referencing dashboard.md)
/docs/dashboard.md (complete Dashboard specs)
Code fixed directly (no separate doc)
/docs/payment-integration.md (if truly a new system)
```

This documentation organization is **NON‑NEGOTIABLE** and must be followed by all contributors to maintain clarity and maintainability for DermAI V2.

---

# 🧬 DermAI V2–Specific Rules

## 🏥 **Dermatological Compliance**

### **Non‑Negotiable Medical Principles**
- ❌ **NEVER medical diagnosis** — Stay within the cosmetic realm
- ❌ **NEVER anxiety‑inducing terms**: “disease”, “pathology”, “medical treatment”
- ✅ **Always use**: “care”, “improvement”, “optimization”, “beauty routine”
- ✅ **Scientific validation**: Respect the 28‑day cell cycle in the phase logic

### **Allowed/Forbidden Vocabulary**
```
❌ FORBIDDEN                      ✅ ALLOWED
“Your skin is damaged”       →   “Your skin shows areas to optimize”
“Medical treatment”          →   “Targeted care”
“Skin pathology”             →   “Beauty concern”
“Medical diagnosis”          →   “Personalized analysis”
```

## 🎨 **UI/UX Consistency**

### **Mandatory Design System**
- **Colors**: Palette defined in `spec.md` section 6.1.1
- **Typography**: Inter for UI, Neue Haas Grotesk for branding
- **Components**: Reuse existing components in `/src/components/`
- **Responsive**: Mobile‑first required

### **Interface Rules**
- **Phase numbering**: Always 1, 2, 3… per phase (never 100, 200…)
- **Temporal badges**: Consistent icons ☀️🌙📈⚡
- **Messages**: Kind and expert tone, never anxiety‑inducing
- **Loading states**: Always provide loading states

## 🤖 **AI Logic & Prompts**

### **Routine Generation**
- **Mandatory 3 phases**: Immediate → Adaptation → Maintenance
- **Intelligent transitions**: Durable base identified and preserved
- **Visual criteria**: Never arbitrary timing; always observable criteria
- **Deduplication**: Avoid duplicate products in the schedule view

### **GPT‑4o Vision Prompts**
- **Non‑directive**: “Analyze objectively” vs “Look for ingrown hairs”
- **Adaptive**: Prompt by user profile (age, gender, skin type)
- **Consistent scoring**: Dynamic weighting by context
- **Safety thresholds**: Never > 85/100 if uncertain; suggest consultation if severe

## 🔧 **Technical Architecture**

### **Mandatory Code Structure**
```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js 15 App Router pages
├── components/       # Reusable components
│   ├── forms/        # Forms and questionnaires
│   ├── results/      # Results display
│   ├── shared/       # Shared components
│   └── upload/       # Photo upload
├── services/         # Business logic
│   ├── ai/           # AI services
│   ├── affiliate/    # Product affiliation
│   └── educational/  # Educational interface
├── types/            # TypeScript types
└── utils/            # Utilities
```

### **Naming Convention**
- **Components**: PascalCase (`AnalysisService`, `PhotoUploadZone`)
- **Files**: kebab-case (`analysis.service.ts`, `photo-upload-zone.tsx`)
- **Variables**: camelCase (`beautyAssessment`, `routineSteps`)
- **Types**: PascalCase with suffix (`UnifiedRoutineStep`, `BeautyAssessment`)

### **Mandatory Performance**
- **Images**: Automatic compression by count (see `utils/images/compressForAPI.ts`)
- **API**: 30s timeout, graceful error handling
- **Bundle**: Route-based code splitting, lazy‑load heavy components
- **Types**: Strict TypeScript, no `any`

## 📱 **Mobile‑First**

### **Responsive Design**
- **Breakpoints**: `sm:` (640px), `md:` (768px), `lg:` (1024px), `xl:` (1280px)
- **Touch‑friendly**: Buttons min 44px, adequate spacing
- **Mobile performance**: WebP images, aggressive compression
- **Offline**: IndexedDB for cache, graceful degradation

### **Mobile Export**
- **Fixed format**: 512×512 px for social networks
- **Quality**: High‑DPI, DermAI logo visible
- **Content**: Condensed yet readable, professional branding

## 💰 **Affiliation & Business**

### **Internal Catalog**
- **Curated products**: Never generic products (“Adapted targeted care”)
- **Real prices**: Always show prices and purchase links
- **Tracking**: Analytics events for conversions
- **Fallback**: If external API fails, use internal catalog

### **Recommendations**
- **Contextual**: By age, budget, skin type, preferences
- **Avoid overdosing**: Max 5 products per routine
- **Transparency**: Indicate if a link is an affiliate link

## 🧪 **Testing & Validation**

### **Mandatory Tests**
- **Unit tests**: Critical services (`analysis.service.ts`, phase calculations)
- **E2E tests**: Full flow upload → diagnosis → routine
- **Mobile testing**: All devices, export working
- **Performance**: Lighthouse mobile score > 90

### **Dermatological Validation**
- **Test cases**: Varied profiles (young/mature, male/female, sensitive)
- **Score consistency**: Delta vs expert < 10%
- **Phase timing**: Validate durations by profile
- **Feedback loop**: Collect user feedback

## 🌍 **Internationalization**

### **i18n Readiness**
- **Externalized texts**: No hard‑coded strings
- **Date formats**: Locale‑aware
- **Responsive text**: Handle variable lengths
- **RTL ready**: Right‑to‑left compatible structure

### **Accessibility (A11y)**
- **ARIA labels**: Label interactive components
- **Contrast**: Minimum AA (4.5:1)
- **Keyboard navigation**: All flows navigable by keyboard
- **Screen readers**: Semantically structured content

## 📊 **Analytics & Tracking**

### **Critical Events**
- `photo_uploaded`: Photos analyzed
- `questionnaire_completed`: Questionnaire finished
- `analysis_completed`: Diagnosis generated
- `product_clicked`: Product interaction
- `routine_viewed`: Routine viewed by phase
- `export_mobile`: Mobile sharing

### **Privacy‑First**
- **GDPR compliant**: Explicit consent
- **Data minimization**: Collect the bare minimum
- **Anonymization**: No personally identifying data
- **Retention**: Automatic purge of old data

---

**These rules complement the documentation organization and ensure the quality, consistency, and compliance of the DermAI V2 project.**
